{
  "title": "Remove AI title/description rewrites from pipeline snapshots",
  "description": "PR #559 dropped AI-suggested tags from pipeline snapshots \
because they churn across machines whenever the AI cache differs. The same \
problem remains for the other two AI enrichments that assemble_snapshot \
(cli/src/pipeline/snapshots.rs) folds into snapshots: enrich_normalize_title \
overrides the snapshot's title and enrich_generate_description overrides its \
description. Both are AI calls, so two machines with different \
~/.ramekin/ai-cache contents produce different committed snapshots even with \
identical code and scrape cache. (The AI-cache poisoning incident on \
2026-06-11 made this vivid: descriptions flipped to mock text purely from \
cache state.)\n\
\n\
Fix: stop reading enrich_normalize_title and enrich_generate_description in \
assemble_snapshot, so snapshots carry only the extracted title/description. \
After this, FinalRecipe is fully deterministic given the scrape cache: \
extraction and ingredient parsing are pure functions of the cached HTML. \
build_final_recipe's normalized_title/generated_description parameters can \
likely go away entirely (FinalRecipe is snapshot-only).\n\
\n\
Related committed outputs that stay non-deterministic and may deserve their \
own pass (probably separate changes): data/tag-report.md is entirely \
AI-derived, and data/extraction-report.md's 'AI Cache' hit/miss counts and \
'Completed' counts vary with per-machine cache state (enrichment failures \
count against completion). The title-normalization and description-generation \
eval reports under data/ have the same property.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "task",
